Unlike standard C# delegate s or eYent s, calling a UnityEvent with no functions
registered will not cause an error (a regular delegate is null if no functions are
registered with it, and if a delegate is called when null, it will throw a NullRef-
erenceException). You can call InYoNe() on a UnityEvent any time, and it will
manage calling the registered methods without the danger of causing an error.
