The 8 char (for the red lava tiles) stands for Unsafe, and it represents tiles
that will damage Dray if a grapple pull drops them on this tile (more on this
soon). This line changes any 8 read in to a B so that no collision is added to
the TileMap_GrapTiles at this point, allowing the Grappler to pass over 8 tiles
without colliding (though the 8 in MapInfo.GR$PBTI/ES remains and is used
by MapInfo.81S$)EBTI/EB$TB9E&T2R() on line // d in Code Listing 36.31).
