public, any class could get the RigidbodyD and &olliderD components of the
Dray GameObject and set any public fields on those components. No code we could
write would prevent this. Instead, we give other classes an easy way to enable or disable
these components through the physicsEnabled property on Dray, and then if this
ever seems to be happening when you don't want it to, you can run the debugger with
a breakpoint in the set clause of physicsEnabled and use this to analyze every time
that physicsEnabled is being set. If other classes were to directly modify the values
on RigidbodyD or &olliderD components, then it would not be possible to easily
watch for those changes in the debugger.
